@--[end]. From which it was evident, that Heaven in the complex is an image of God; and an image of God is a form of Divine order.

@66. When the inmost sight (of the Angels) is opened, they recognise their own image in (the surrounding objects)... Therefore, images of their affections are thus presented.

@459[17]. Ho, therefore, who loves justice from the Lord, and does it with judgment, is charity in its image and likeness.

@500. It is the Primary of order, that man should become an image of God...

@767[2]. For all evil is in a certain form the image of its reigning love; and the falsity thence presents this image as in a mirror.

